sic and the slow  panning shots it's just one of those  gritty tense battles that can even stand  to be a bit bloodier to drive the point  home  speaking of ensemble fights domain vs  valhalla is really epic  yep this is something that i'd expect  from tokyo revenge's good old gang wars  that have no shortage of fierce action  and drama the fights between the mob are  all sorts of intense but the camera's  all focused on the meat of the action i  really find the camera cuts in their  individual fights so well done you can  feel that you're part of the action by  just watching and seeing how each of  their fast blows gets captured in anime  forms but it was mikey scene that stole  the show for me the tension and the  drama was an all-time high and it looks  like one of dorman's pillars finally bit  the dust until he didn't i got  goosebumps seeing mikey get back up and  hand everyone else a whole can of ass  kicking he's down but he's never out and  all it takes is a switch being flipped  for him to go all bad ass and raise hell  all over the enemies  rin versus nickel from either then  deities is also pretty cool  at first i wasn't too sure what to  expect from this late coming to the  season the premise is simple enough but  i didn't think that either then dt's had  a premise that lends itself to a lot of  attention grabbing battles the synopsis  partially thanks to the art reads more  like a comedy with a few dashes of nice  fights nice but pretty standard and not  too great i'm glad to have been proven  wrong though especially with this fight  between rin and nickel or should i say  rin's showcase of power the fight looks  unique compared to the rest of the  roster so fighting that it retains the  light cartoony appeal of ida den deity's  art it doesn't look as crisp or modern  as something like the siesta fight that  started this list regardless the fight  has that same appeal that those chinese  anime fights that i love so much had in  that despite the simplistic art style  it's got that wacky cartoony feel that  you might just enjoy  [Music]  it feels so good to have madoka magika  once again the new movie looms in the  horizon and the second half of magyar  record finally kicks the plot into  overdrive after what the first season  left us in particular i really loved  seeing our favorite magical girls in  action again and margie our record does  an excellent job of introducing new  characters and having them work with or  face off against the legacy characters i  always felt that mommy would have been a  great villain and she displays that  pedigree in full glory in this fight  against everyone her bullet hell  abilities always steal the show and  fighting without restraint as a villain  it becomes even more of a treat to watch  suruno has her own issues with the  protagonists and it's nice to see the  two groups of battles converge into one  chaotic display of explosions and magic  the fight also has quite the emotional  backdrop to it and while margie a record  may not have quite captured the success  of its predecessor this season 2 has  more than redeemed season 1 for me  there's a lot more at stake and far  better action  a featured castlevania fight often in  these videos so i think that the witcher  deserves a mention too  [Music]  it's not anime in the traditional sense  but the anime version of the witcher has  had some highlights of its own one such  highlight is chetra vs vesamir while i  won't say that the fight carries the  entire movie and makes it an absolute  must-watch it's also an absolute treat  that shows off what non-japan animation  can do fans also agree that jetra is one  of the great antagonists in this list  that greatly expands the lore of the  games this fight really sold me to her  as a character and it felt so good  seeing the two combatants go back and  forth inside the crammed space amidst  the fires the witch anime is good  supplementary material to the game and  the tv show so if you are a fan make  sure to check it out the movie still is  pretty good in its own right so that's  probably a point of consideration for  you too  my hero academia continues rolling with  shigeraki vs redestro  my villain academia hitting all the  right notes in the decisive  confrontation between the two leaders of  the villainous factions a lot of people  have been clamoring to see shigaraki and  redestro duking it out in anime form and  while that fight's been toned down it  still does manage to be a home run  villain versus villain showdowns have  always been interesting because it's a  battle that you can sit back and not be  too invested on one side or it should  have been what happens is that a lot of  these end up having one less bad guy for  you to root for in this case i found  myself rooting for shigaraki more due to  how much better he is as a character for  me but none of that matters when we  start seeing the fireworks flight and  the city being destroyed in a clash that  would put some of the previous mha  battles to shame with two characters who  have less of a moral compass duking it  out you'd expect to see carnage and  destruction and that's exactly what we  got in the end shigeraki stands  victorious after leaving a lot of  annihilation in his wake capping off the  ark that ended up being a lot more  interesting than i first expected it to  be when it was still in its anime form  should i also point out that both of  their powers show some similarities to  deku's and overhauls powers talk about  irony and a callback to one of the best  fights of the previous my hero academia  him  you think that these slice of life  dragons can throw it down but here we  are doru and elmar just had an intense  battle that could give some shonen  fights a run for their money thoru and  elma blast each other with attacks that  just make you go wow seeing each blast  that sends the combatants flying miles  away is a joy but i love the banter more  in-fight talking helps drives up the  stakes and the intensity of a fight and  the voice actors show us a better way  than expected example of that here it  also gave us a surprisingly touching  scene between the combatants which i  feel is the more important takeaway here  fights are not just all about the energy  blasts and the punches after all the  emotion has to be there as well on the  meta side of things what makes this  sequence so touching is that it's  something created in-house in kyoto  animation the whole sequence is the  staff flexing their skills and  delivering with a product that's a lot  better than what we can ask for shows a  lot about the resiliency of one of the  best studios in the industry all things  considered in spite of the tragedy a few  years ago kyoto animation has come back  stronger and i find that a very  wholesome thing  coming up next is naruto vs ishiki  [Applause]  ishiki's been having naruto's number for  the longest time he already did the  unthinkable and beat both naruto and  sasuke and he looks to be in the process  of doing so again this time naruto has a  new form but will it be able to turn the  tides we're talking about a new form in  shonen anime so what do you expect new  forms may not win all the time but they  sure look good doing so almost all the  time barry on mode ends up being  impressive with it all allowing naruto  to bring the beat down to ishiki  smacking him around and drawing lots of  clean hits that would have taken out any  lesser being all while looking all kinds  of sleek thanks to the huge makeover it  doesn't come without a price though as  both he and ishiki will soon realize as  the battle wears on this entry is a late  edition that came up as i was in the  process of wrapping up the video script  but it's very worth the spot you can  really feel the impact from each of  naruto's blows and with the rocky music  keeping you pumped up the battle is a  treat to watch hand-to-hand combat has  rarely looked this good but the guys  behind boruto did it the adaptation  really did justice to the hype  so how would you rank these 10 fights  though i'm curious to see which one  you'd put on top of a hypothetical list  if you had a great time and one more  don't forget to check out the channel  for the past videos that you may have  missed after checking those out you can  head over to the members only videos and  consider applying for channel membership  my patreon is also in the description  box in case you really want to help me  make more amazing videos and your help  would be one of the best things i could  possibly get that's it for today's list  i hope to see you again next time and  i'll be back with more anime countdowns  see ya  [Music]  you

